<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Enchelei</h1><p class="st-meta">700 BCE – 300 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Illyrian people around Lake Ohrid, linked by Greek legend to the hero Cadmus, among the earliest Illyrian groups named in Greek sources.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Greek writers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hecataeus-of-miletus">Hecataeus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> onward place the Enchelei, the 'eel people', near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ohrid">Lake Ohrid</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drin">Drin</a> valley. Myth said <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadmus">Cadmus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harmonia">Harmonia</a> came to rule them after leaving <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>, and that their descendants ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyrians">Illyrians</a>. Little beyond these mentions survives, and their origins are otherwise unknown.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from scattered Greek references, the Enchelei appear as a tribal people of the lake district around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrid">Lychnidus</a> (Ohrid), whose fisheries probably gave them their name. Later authors seem to treat the Sesarethii as the same or a successor people.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the 4th century BCE their name fades, and the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ohrid">Lake Ohrid</a> appears under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dassaretae">Dassaretae</a> and within the sphere of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/illyrian-kingdom">Illyrian Kingdom</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 700 BCE – 300 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:45.77%;width:7.96%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 BCE – 300 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Illyrian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Illyrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Encheleans, Sesarethii</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-500&amp;focus=enchelei" aria-label="Enchelei on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5173 725 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Enchelei lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5493 981h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5493 981h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Albania. <a href="/atlas?year=-500&amp;focus=enchelei">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

